{
  "assembly_notes": "A carpenter's folding rule generalised from the source two-blade angle ruler. Four orthogonal, freely composable structural slots: hinge_style (pivot hardware at every joint), end_profile (segment pivot-end mesh), blade_section (slat cross-section family) and tip_treatment (the two free chain ends). segment_count (N) is the multiplicity, item_slot=end_profile: N graduated segments joined by N-1 out-of-plane (Z-axis) revolute hinges. The chain is serial (segment_0 is the supported root, hinge_i parents segment_i to segment_{i+1}). Rotation is about Z only, so each segment keeps a fixed stacked Z level (i*level_pitch_m) at every fold angle and bodies never intersect; the per-joint through-rivet hub captures the child near lug with a 0.3 mm retention seat (no overlap allowance). blade_section and tip_treatment share ONE section descriptor (section_rise_m, section_drop_m, section_flat_x0_m, section_feature_width_m): it drives the blade mesh, level_pitch_m = thickness_m + section_rise_m + section_drop_m + style_gap_m, hence the hub seat child_lug_top_z_m and the hub axle length, and the graduation land (band_center_x_m / band_width_m). Every raised feature is confined to the mid-span window outside the pivot-hub keepout (DIAL_FACE_R + 0.005), so no cross-section relief can reach under a hub. core_domain = 2 x 2 x 3 x 3 = 36, raw_domain = 180.",
